{
 "brief": "Aid deliveries to Gaza dropped sharply in September, the Shehab Wire reported. The number of assistance trucks entering the enclave through the Kerem Shalom crossing fell 43 percent compared to August, according to the agency's figures.\n\nThe decline comes as humanitarian needs intensify across the territory. More than 95 percent of Gaza's population relies on aid, making the reduction significant amid an escalating crisis.",
